          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most tractor owners, the Agri-Fab 45-0492 is the lawn sweeper to buy: its 5.6:1 brush ratio handles heavier debris than the rest, the flow-through bag uses its full volume, and the offset hitch lets you mow and sweep at once. On an acre or more, the Ohio Steel 50SWP26 trades a little brush speed for a wider path and a clog-resistant chute. If you will use a sweeper all season, the Brinly's side-mounted height adjustment makes it the easiest to live with.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Without a tractor, a push sweeper is only worth it on small, flat lawns. Buy the steel Agri-Fab 45-0570 if you want it to last. And if your leaves are usually wet or your leaf fall is modest, save the money and mulch them with your mower instead.
